{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And you shall make the boards for the Tabernacle, etc.</b> 'The boards' — with the definite article — means those cedar trees that Jacob planted for them in Egypt. A sign for the matter: 'הַקְּרָשִׁים לַמִּשְׁכָּן' has the numerical value of 'יַעֲקֹב אָבִינוּ נָטַע לָהֶם אֲרָזִים בְּמִצְרַיִם' — for the numerical value of both is תתרצ״ה. For Jacob said to the Holy One, blessed be He: 'With what will You be appeased for the deed of the calf?' And the Holy One, blessed be He, answered him: 'With acacia wood.' And so it is found in the Midrash: acacia wood (עֲצֵי שִׁטִּים) to atone for the folly (שְׁטוּת) of the deed of the calf, and it will be appeased for them as atonement before HaShem. And so he concludes in Tanḥuma (Terumah 10). And in tractate Yoma (72a) they expounded what is written, 'עֲצֵי שִׁטִּים עֹמְדִים' — that they stand forever. But according to the plain sense, that Jacob prepared them for the service of the house of our Elohim, we may say that therefore it says 'עֹמְדִים' — to say that they should take from those acacia woods that were standing prepared for this, for this is the meaning of the term 'עֹמְדִים' in many places, for something prepared and standing ready for that purpose. And the allusion in these cedars comes to what is stated (Psalms 92:13): 'צַדִּיק כַּתָּמָר יִפְרָח, כְּאֶרֶז בַּלְּבָנוֹן יִשְׂגֶּה' — 'The righteous flourishes like a palm tree; like a cedar in Lebanon he grows great.' And since the body of the righteous is likened to this cedar, therefore HaShem, blessed be He, caused His Shekhinah to dwell within partitions of cedar wood — to teach by a fortiori reasoning that He dwells also among the children of Israel, who are likened to cedars by water, as it is written (Exodus 25:8): 'וְשָׁכַנְתִּי בְּתוֹכָם' — 'בְּתוֹכוֹ' is not said, but rather 'בְּתוֹכָם,' to say that the essential indwelling of the Shekhinah is for Israel's sake. And Ba'al ha-Turim explained: forty-eight boards corresponding to forty-eight prophets, and forty-eight priestly and Levitical watches — and what is their connection to the boards if not because the righteous is likened to a cedar as stated?" "And Rabbeinu Jacob Ba'al ha-Turim further wrote that in this parashah we find twenty-four occurrences of 'shittim' corresponding to the twenty-four thousand who fell at Shittim (Numbers 25:9). And the reason for the matter is that every place where you find a boundary against immorality, there you find holiness. And since at Shittim they were wanton in sexual immorality and did not take heed of the holiness of these twenty-four 'shittim' occurrences, therefore twenty-four thousand fell. And in parashat Balak, with Elohim's help, a precious reason for the number twenty-four thousand will be explained, on the verse (Numbers 23:3): 'וְאָנֹכִי אִקָּרֶה כֹּה' — let it be sought in its place."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {1 "The phrase 'בע״ה' expands to 'בעזרת השם' (with Elohim's help); rendered accordingly."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:23:34.593621182Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}